      "writtenOn": "2026-06-03T10:29:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, it would be extremely easy to adapt in the future.\n\nBecause this branch abstracts the threading model behind the dispatcher property and the execute { ... } block (which just uses withContext(dispatcher)), the call sites don\u0027t need to know how the thread is managed.\n\nIf the Dawn native APIs become thread-safe in the future, all we have to do is change the createDefaultWebGpuDispatcher() function from returning a single-threaded executor to returning a multi-threaded one (like Dispatchers.Default or a larger thread pool). The withContext(dispatcher) blocks throughout the codebase would instantly start executing concurrently across multiple threads without requiring us to rewrite the actual WebGPU logic or remove any manual mutexes.",
      "parentUuid": "d3cadc95_8a593dac",
      "revId": "f65e15f160c424579edc31b6a72ab61ef6f4e0fb",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
